<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrés Manuel López Obrador</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as AMLO</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrés Manuel López Obrador is a Mexican politician who was president from 2018 to 2024. A former head of government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> and twice a losing presidential candidate, he founded the Morena party and won a landslide in 2018 on promises to fight corruption and poverty. His government expanded social programmes and the state's role in energy, and his ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudia-sheinbaum">Claudia Sheinbaum</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andres-manuel-lopez-obrador.jpg" alt="Andrés Manuel López Obrador" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EneasMx · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andr%C3%A9s_Manuel_L%C3%B3pez_Obrador_junio_2024.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
